# Step 2 works here. Two kinds of file live in this directory and only one of
# them is derived (SPEC 3.1). Patterns are anchored with a leading slash so
# they match only this directory, never a like-named file further down.

# Copied here by hand from merge/merged.csv - see merge/README.md.
/merged.csv

# Written by ./import.sh profile.
/profile.md
/profile.json

# Schema stanzas proposed for a human to apply (SPEC 3.4).
/proposals.md

# Tracked, and must stay tracked: mapping.yaml and value_map.yaml are
# hand-edited and are the whole manual step of the import, and id_map.csv is
# what keeps project ids stable across re-imports. Losing any of them means
# redoing the mapping or renaming every project.
#
# example-extract.csv is tracked too: it is invented demo data, not a real
# extract, so committing it does not touch SPEC 12.8. README.md walks the
# import through with it.

import-report.md
